  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_14' aria-label=\" Sandeep Singh Bora versus Narendra Singh Deopa & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('14','2026','2026_2_257_269','2026INSC105'); ><font size='4'> <strong>SANDEEP SINGH BORA<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>NARENDRA SINGH DEOPA & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 2 S.C.R. 257</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 105</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000412026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : VIKRAM NATH<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SANDEEP MEHTA</strong><br> Issue for Consideration The instant appeal is directed against the interim order dated 18.07.2025 passed by the High Court wherein it directed the Returning Officer to allot a symbol to respondent no.1 (the writ petitioner) and permit him to participate in the election to the office of Zila &ndash; Art.243-O &ndash; Uttarakhand Panchayati Raj Act, 2016 &ndash; The Uttarakhand State Election Commission issued a revised notification resuming the Panchayat elections in the State &ndash; Pursuant thereto, respondent no.1 submitted his nomination for election to the post of Zila<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 02-02-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 691/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Case Allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('14','2026','2026_2_257_269','2026INSC105','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href